WPR23LA901.factual:
The commercial pilot was flying the airplane on a skydiving flight with 12 parachutists on board. The pilot reported that, during the climb through about 6,000 ft mean sea level, the engine lost power.

{{fill:long-skyd}}

Postaccident examination of the engine, including a teardown at the manufacturer, revealed no anomalies that would have precluded normal operation.
